<BaseLayout title="About — Bolan Xu"><section class="page-head"><div class="container"><div class="eyebrow">ABOUT / THE PERSON BEHIND THE BENCH</div><h1>HI, I'M<br/>BOLAN.</h1></div></section><article class="container content prose"><p>I like figuring out how things work, then building my own version.</p><p>Most of what I make lives somewhere between electronics, embedded systems, software, robotics, and an unreasonable amount of debugging.</p><h2>How I got here</h2><p>I started making things because it was more interesting than just using them. A simple radio turned into robots, circuits, software, and eventually projects like Terminus—a phone designed around the idea of communication without the usual smartphone baggage.</p><h2>What I use</h2><div class="project-meta"><div class="spec"><span class="spec-label">Hardware</span><span class="spec-value">PCBs · Microcontrollers · Sensors</span></div><div class="spec"><span class="spec-label">Software</span><span class="spec-value">C/C++ · Python · Web</span></div><div class="spec"><span class="spec-label">Robotics</span><span class="spec-value">ROS 2 · Control · Computer Vision</span></div><div class="spec"><span class="spec-label">Currently</span><span class="spec-value">Building things</span></div></div></article></BaseLayout>
